1.bug_scenario:
When you enable the ESLint “key-spacing” rule with “multiLine: { align: 'value' }” and run “eslint --fix” on a JSX file containing inline style={{ … }} objects, ESLint will forcibly break your single-line style objects into multiple lines and then mis-align the colons and values. In other words, instead of leaving your compact style={{marginRight: '4px', color: '#0C090A', …}} alone, it expands it to

  style={{
      marginRight:     '4px',
      color:           '#0C090A',
      opacity:         '0.6',
      fontSize:        '18px',
      verticalAlign:   'middle'
  }}

even though you didn’t ask to break it across lines. The result is both a spurious line-break on a single-line object and an ugly re-alignment inside your JSX curly braces.
